#. type: Title #
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Contribute"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Code, bug reports, translations and tests with other printers, cassettes and label rolls are welcome."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Issues and pull requests on [GitHub](https://github.com/joshii-h/etiketto) are welcome, no Forgejo account needed. They are copied automatically to [Forgejo](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto), the main repository, with a link on GitHub. Review and merge happen there; your commits are kept, so GitHub shows the pull request as merged. The discussion can stay on GitHub.  With a Forgejo account you can contribute there directly.  Details: [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto/src/branch/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**App translations**: `tools/strings_<lang>.py`, see CONTRIBUTING."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**This documentation**: `site/po/<lang>.po`, see [site/README.md](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto/src/branch/main/site/README.md).  Names of buttons and settings come from the app translation automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Other printers**: printing goes through a backend interface; a new printer is a new backend. The protocols of the supported printers are described in [docs/](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto/src/branch/main/docs), one file per printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Etiketto"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Etiketto designs labels under Linux and prints them over the network, on endless tape or on die-cut labels. It talks to each printer in its own language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Main window](media/main.png#only-light)  ![Main window](media/main-dark.png#only-dark)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Text, images, QR codes and barcodes; backgrounds printed edge to edge"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Preview at print resolution: what you see is what is printed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Endless tape as long as the content, or die-cut labels of any size"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Finds the printer in the network, reads what is loaded and explains printer problems in plain words"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "27 languages, follows the light or dark mode of the desktop"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The supported printers and what each one can do are listed under [Printers](printer.md). Further printers can be added as a backend, see [Contribute](contribute.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Flatpak"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Flathub is in preparation. Until then, build it yourself:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/index.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git clone https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto.git && cd etiketto\n"
"flatpak install --user flathub org.gnome.Sdk//51 org.gnome.Platform//51\n"
"flatpak-builder --user --install --force-clean build-dir \\\n"
"    build-aux/flatpak/xyz.joshuahirsig.Etiketto.yml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "install.sh"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Install the system packages, then run the script as your user (no root):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Distribution | Packages |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Debian, Ubuntu | `python3-gi gir1.2-gtk-4.0 gir1.2-adw-1 python3-gi-cairo python3-venv gettext` |\n"
"| Fedora | `python3-gobject gtk4 libadwaita python3-cairo gettext` |\n"
"| Arch | `python-gobject gtk4 libadwaita python-cairo gettext` |\n"
"| Gentoo | `dev-python/pygobject gui-libs/gtk:4 gui-libs/libadwaita dev-python/pycairo sys-devel/gettext` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/index.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git clone https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/etiketto.git && cd etiketto\n"
"./install.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Uninstall: `./install.sh --uninstall` or `flatpak uninstall xyz.joshuahirsig.Etiketto`.  Saved labels and templates are kept."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "First label"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Switch the printer on and choose it under [[ui:Printer model]]. Etiketto finds it in the network (Bonjour) and reads what is loaded: the tape width or the distance between the labels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Not found? Enter the address under [[ui:Host name or IP address]], e.g.  `printer.local` or `192.168.1.50`. New printer: connect it to the network first, see [Printers](printer.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Add]] text, an image or a code, then [[ui:Print]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Save]] stores the label as `.etiketto` file, [[ui:Save as template…]] adds it to [[ui:Templates]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Printers and troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose the printer under [[ui:Printer model]]; each one has its own section below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "All printers { #common }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:No printer found]]: printer on and in the same network? The search needs the Avahi service (installed on most desktops, any init system); systemd-resolved alone resolves `.local` names but cannot search. Otherwise enter the address under [[ui:Host name or IP address]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Printer not reachable]]: check the address, the printer may have a new IP. Switch the printer off and on again. On USB: check the cable and search again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "No permission for the USB port: your user needs to be in the group `lp`.  Run `sudo usermod -aG lp $USER`, then log out and in again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "USB printer not found: check the cable, switch the printer on and wake it up (a sleeping printer can drop off USB), then search again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "\"The printer is busy\" on USB: only one program can use a USB printer at a time. Close other label software, or wait until the running print is done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Printer needs attention]]: the printer is reachable but reports a problem, the text below says what to do. Clear it on the printer, then [[ui:Refresh]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Content cut off at the edge or askew: increase the [[ui:Safety margin]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:content scaled down to fit]]: the content does not fit the label.  Make the label longer or larger, use [[ui:Automatic length]] on tape, or shorten the content."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Brother VC-500W { #vc500w }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Wi-Fi setup { #wifi }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Etiketto does not set up Wi-Fi. Use a phone or the printer's web interface once:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Hold the Wi-Fi button until it turns from blue to white."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Connect phone or computer to the open network \"Brother VC-500W…\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open `https://192.168.0.1` (accept the certificate warning) or Brother's Color Label Editor app."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose your network and enter the password. Only 2.4 GHz, WPA or open."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Later, the web interface is at `https://` and the printer's address: \"Network Wi-Fi Setup\" changes the network (or \"click here\" to enter it by hand), \"AirPrint Options\" sets name, location and firmware updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "USB { #vc500w-usb }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Plug the printer in; [[ui:Search for printers]] finds it. Printing over USB has not been tried on a printer yet and follows the observations of others: the printer may not answer over USB at all (then the query ends with [[ui:Printer not reachable]]), and it may not cut by itself, then swipe across its panel. Wi-Fi is the tried way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Cassettes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Cassette | Width |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| CZ-1001 | 9 mm (3/8″) |\n"
"| CZ-1002 | 12 mm (1/2″) |\n"
"| CZ-1003 | 19 mm (3/4″) |\n"
"| CZ-1004 | 25 mm (1″) |\n"
"| CZ-1005 | 50 mm (2″) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Etiketto shows the inserted cassette, remaining tape, printable width, lot number and the presumed production date. ZINK paper ages: old paper prints paler and yellowish, Etiketto warns about old cassettes. Store cassettes cool and dry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Cleaning: insert the cleaning cassette CK-1000, cleaning starts by itself.  Do it when stripes appear, or every 20 to 30 labels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print options { #vc500w-print }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Cut]]: [[ui:Full cut]] separates the labels. [[ui:Half cut]] cuts through the label, the backing holds them together. [[ui:No cut]]: the printer waits, swipe its panel to cut."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Colours]]: [[ui:Vivid]] for the strongest colours, [[ui:Normal]] (Brother: Standard) for softer ones, black and white (400 lpi) for text and codes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Colour correction: brightness and colour balance (red, green, blue), for this print only, not stored in the printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems { #vc500w-problems }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Wrong cassette]]: the label was designed for another width. Change [[ui:Tape width]] or the cassette."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:No cassette inserted]] or cassette not recognised: reinsert the cassette until it clicks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "No paper: the cassette is empty, replace it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Paper jam: open the cover, remove the jammed label, reinsert the cassette."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Cover open: close the cover."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Warming up, cooling down, cleaning: wait, printing continues by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Swipe the panel to cut: the label was printed without cut, swipe across the panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Pale colours, yellow tint: old paper (see the cassette's age), or [[ui:Normal]] instead of [[ui:Vivid]]. With old cassettes try [[ui:Brightness]] −1 to −3 under [[ui:Colour adjustment]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Background barely visible: ZINK hardly prints very light pastel shades, choose a medium shade."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Stripes: clean with the CK-1000."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Content askew: insert the cassette straight."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "cab label printers { #cab }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Etiketto prints on cab printers with a 4 inch print head: EOS2, EOS5, SQUIX 4 and MACH 4S, at 203, 300 or 600 dpi. Developed with an EOS2/300."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Network: the printer needs an address in your network (DHCP or set on its display). Etiketto uses the \"RawIP\" port 9100 with the JScript interpreter, both are the printer's defaults (Setup > Interfaces > Network services and Setup > Interpreter)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "USB: plug the printer in; [[ui:Search for printers]] finds it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Labels: die-cut labels with a gap, label sensor \"Gap Sensor\". Etiketto sets the sensor for each job. Continuous media and a cutter are not supported yet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Print method (thermal direct or with ribbon), heat, speed and tear-off position stay as set on the printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems { #cab-problems }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Different labels loaded]]: the printer measured another distance between the labels than height plus gap of your label. Check [[ui:Label size]] and [[ui:Gap]], or load the right roll. Press Feed on the printer once after changing the roll so it measures again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A print that stopped because of a problem is cancelled, so printing again does not give extra labels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Out of labels: load a new roll, the printer then synchronises by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Print head open: close the print head."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Next label not found: labels not threaded through the label sensor, or labels without gaps (continuous media is not supported yet)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ribbon problem: no ribbon in thermal transfer mode, or a ribbon in thermal direct mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Paused: resume the printer on its display."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Print too pale or too dark: change the heat level in the printer's setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "System printer (CUPS, IPP) { #system }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Prints on the printers your computer knows: printers set up in the system settings (also over USB) and printers in the network that support IPP Everywhere or AirPrint, as most office printers do. The label is printed as one page of exactly its size, unscaled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Search for printers]] lists both. Otherwise enter the printer's address or the name of its CUPS queue under [[ui:Host name or IP address]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Label size]]: the paper size, or [[ui:Custom size]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Print on]] [[ui:Label sheet]]: several labels on a sheet of self-adhesive labels, see [Label sheets](sheets.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Most office printers cannot print the outer 4 to 5 mm of a page: set the [[ui:Safety margin]] to 5 mm. On label sheets Etiketto warns when a label reaches into what the printer reports."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems { #system-problems }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Out of paper, paper jam or cover open while printing: Etiketto shows it and waits. Fix it at the printer within 5 minutes and printing goes on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Out of toner or ink, or a problem before printing: fix it as the printer's display shows, then [[ui:Refresh]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Printing fails after some copies: the message says how many labels were already printed. The rest is canceled, nothing prints later on its own."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The label is printed smaller or moved: the printer or its driver scales the page. Turn off \"fit to page\" in the printer's setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Other jobs are printing first: Etiketto says the label was sent, and the printer prints it when its turn comes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The job is held in the queue (until it is released, or until a password is entered): Etiketto cancels it. Check the queue in the system settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Help"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Something else? [[ui:Report a problem…]] in the main menu (also offered with error messages) opens a prefilled issue in the browser with version, system and printer. You see everything before sending it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Label sheets { #sheets }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "With the [[ui:System printer (CUPS, IPP)]], an office printer prints on sheets of self-adhesive labels: A4 or US Letter pages with a grid of labels, as Avery, Zweckform, Herma and many others sell them. Etiketto knows more than 1700 of these sheets, from the template collection of gLabels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the sheet { #choose }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Printer model]]: [[ui:System printer (CUPS, IPP)]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Print on]]: [[ui:Label sheet]]. The list of sheets opens."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Search by brand and part number as printed on the package (\"Avery L7160\", \"Zweckform 3475\"), or by the size of one label in millimetres (\"70x37\", either way round). The paper size narrows the list down."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The picture shows the sheet; [[ui:Use sheet]] takes it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The label now has the size of the sheet's labels. Round labels and CDs are designed as a rectangle, and printed only inside their shape; the preview shows them that way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Turn the content]]: for labels read from the side, such as folder spines: the label is designed lying on its side and turned onto the sheet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Print on]]: [[ui:Single label]] prints the label as a page of its own again; choosing [[ui:Label sheet]] again brings back the last sheet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Partly used sheets { #positions }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Positions]] shows the sheet. Click a label to leave it out (it is already used) or to print on it again, or set [[ui:Start at position]]: the labels are counted row by row from the top left. This only applies to the first sheet; further sheets are filled completely. The sheet and the positions are saved with the label."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print { #print }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Labels]]: how many labels to print. At first as many as positions are chosen; more fill further sheets. The dialog shows how many sheets that takes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Print outlines]]: prints the outline of every label. Print a test page on plain paper first and hold it against a label sheet in front of a light: if the content sits inside the outlines, the sheet fits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Office printers cannot print near the paper's edges. Etiketto asks the printer for that margin and warns if the content of a label (inside the [[ui:Safety margin]]) reaches into it. Leave those positions out, or increase the [[ui:Safety margin]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The paper size comes from the sheet; turn off \"fit to page\" in the printer's setup, otherwise the printer may scale the sheet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sheets.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The sheet templates come from gLabels (© Jaye Evins, MIT license)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Design and print"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Content"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Elements are placed one after another along the label. Order them with [[ui:Move up]] and [[ui:Move down]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Editing a text element](media/expand.png#only-light)  ![Editing a text element](media/expand-dark.png#only-dark)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Text**: any installed font, colour, several lines. [[ui:Size]] 0 fills the label height, otherwise fixed in pt."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Image**: photos and graphics; drag and drop works too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Symbol**: a pictogram from the symbol library, see below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Code**: [[ui:Type]] offers 2D codes (QR code, Data Matrix, PDF417, Aztec), linear barcodes (Code 128, Code 39, Code 93, EAN-13, EAN-8, UPC-A, UPC-E, ITF-14) and GS1 codes (GS1-128, GS1 DataMatrix). Below the type it says what the type is for and what it accepts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "EAN, UPC and ITF-14: enter the digits without the check digit, it is added; with it, it is checked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "GS1-128 and GS1 DataMatrix: application identifiers in brackets, each followed by its value, e.g. `(01)09501101530003(17)261231(10)AB12`.  Etiketto checks identifiers, lengths, dates and check digits and says which identifier is wrong. GS1-128 shows the identifiers in brackets below the bars."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A GS1 value with round brackets in it: write the identifiers in square brackets, e.g. `[01]09501101530003[21]A(B)C`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "ITF-14 and GS1-128 on shipping cartons: GS1 asks for modules of at least 0.495 mm. On narrow labels they come out narrower: fine for your own scanners, too small for carton labels read in logistics."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Code 39: a `$`, `/`, `+` or `%` before a capital letter is read as another character by scanners set to Full ASCII; Etiketto warns."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Content a code type cannot take is not changed silently: the element is crossed out and a warning says why."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Labels with a code type other than QR code, Code 128 and EAN-13 do not open in earlier versions of Etiketto: they say the label needs a newer version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Codes print sharp on every printer: each bar and square is a whole number of printer dots, as close to the designed width as the element's space allows, with the blank margin a scanner needs. The code may come out slightly smaller than designed, centred in its space."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A code whose bars are only one printer dot wide, or without room for its blank margin, may not scan: Etiketto warns before printing, make the code larger. A code that does not fit at all is not printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "QR codes with characters beyond plain ASCII (umlauts, °, £ …) are now marked as UTF-8, so scanners read them correctly. Labels made with earlier versions print such a QR code with a slightly different pattern."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Labels made with earlier versions: QR codes come out up to about a third smaller (their blank margin is now inside the element), barcodes slightly wider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Symbols"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Symbol…]] opens the symbol library: over 7000 pictograms such as arrows, warnings, recycling, tools, food or weather, from Material Design Icons. Search by name, for example \"arrow\" or \"recycle\". The names and categories come from the icon set and are English, so the search is in English too. The list next to the search shows one category; [[ui:Recently used]] shows the symbols chosen last. The \"Brand / Logo\" category and further icons showing brands or trademarks are left out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Size]] 0 fills the label height, otherwise the symbol has this height."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Rotation]]: a quarter turn at a time, clockwise."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The colour is printed on colour and office printers. Black-and-white label printers print symbols in black, or in white if the colour is light, with sharp edges."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The label file keeps the outline of each symbol, so a label looks the same in later versions. Older versions of Etiketto cannot open labels with symbols and say that the label needs a newer version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Label"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Endless tape:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Automatic length]]: the label is as long as its content. Off: fixed [[ui:Length]], content aligned and scaled down if needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "For every label:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Spacing]]: space at the ends and between elements."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Edge spacing]]: extra space along the label edges."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Background colour]], [[ui:Background image]]: printed edge to edge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Border]]: width, 0 = none; always inside the safety margin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Units]]: millimetres or inches, by default from the system language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Die-cut labels have a fixed size instead of a length:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Die-cut label](media/die-cut.png#only-light)  ![Die-cut label](media/die-cut-dark.png#only-dark)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Label size]]: a common size, or [[ui:Custom size]] with [[ui:Width]] (across the roll) and [[ui:Height]] (along the roll), as on the label box."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Gap]]: space between two labels on the roll, usually 2 to 3 mm.  Before printing Etiketto compares height and gap with the distance the printer measured."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Content direction]]: [[ui:Across the roll]] for labels read with the roll running from top to bottom, [[ui:Along the roll]] like on tape."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Alignment]]: where the content sits if it is shorter than the label."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Safety margin]] (printer setting, default 1.5 mm): content and border keep this distance from the label edges. Printers lose a little at the edges, and long labels can run slightly askew. If text is cut off at the edge, increase it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shipping labels"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Carriers and marketplaces send shipping labels as a PDF or an image, often an A4 page with the label in one half or quarter and a receipt or instructions next to it. [[ui:Shipping label…]] in the main menu (or a PDF dropped onto the window) opens such a file and makes a new label of it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Etiketto looks for the label on the page: a large area with the shape of a label, best with a printed frame and a barcode; a page with one label filling it is taken whole. Check the selection: drag it, drag its edges, or draw a new one. [[ui:Next suggestion]] shows other areas that could be the label, [[ui:Whole page]] selects all of it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Page]]: the page of a PDF with several pages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Label size]]: 4 × 6 in (101.6 × 152.4 mm), 100 × 150 mm, 100 × 200 mm, a 62 mm roll that is as long as the label needs, or A6 and A4 paper on the system printer. Only sizes the printer can print are offered; on endless tape the label runs along the tape."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A label printed sideways on the page is turned upright for the size; [[ui:Rotate left]] and [[ui:Rotate right]] turn it by hand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Scale]]: [[ui:Whole area, centred]] keeps all of the area, [[ui:Fill the label, edges cut off]] fills the label completely."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Create label]] replaces the open label. The area stays an element of the label: [[ui:Area]] in its row opens the selection again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A PDF page is drawn right at the resolution it is printed at, without smoothing: bars and text come out as whole dots, so barcodes stay readable. Lines thinner than a dot are printed at least one dot wide (sometimes two), and in black even if they are light grey or coloured; white lines thinner than a dot on black may vanish. Label printers get the label at their own resolution. The system printer gets it without loss: as PWG Raster drawn at the printer's resolution, or as a PDF drawn at 300 dpi, which a printer of another resolution scales itself (on a 203 dpi printer the edges of bars may then soften: check that the barcode scans).  Only printers that take nothing but JPEG get a compressed copy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Images are enlarged by repeating pixels, evenly only by whole multiples (otherwise some pixels come out one dot wider than others); reduced, the pixels that fall together are averaged into grey."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "On black-and-white printers the area is looked at piece by piece. Where it is black and white but for grey edges (barcodes and text, also from a scan with grey ink on grey paper), it is cut at the middle between its own black and white, so bars keep clean edges; images are enlarged smoothly for this, so the edges fall between the pixels of the scan.  Where it has grey of its own (a grey logo, grey text down to light grey, a shaded band), the grey is printed as a dot pattern; black text on it gets a narrow edge of paper so that it stays readable. A scan or photo of a label should have at least 150 dpi; at 100 dpi only a clean one keeps all its bars."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The label file keeps the whole page the area was taken from, also outside the area (addresses, tracking numbers). Of a PDF with several pages only the chosen page is kept if it can be copied unchanged, otherwise the whole document (the dialog then says so). Unchanged is strict: a copy that differs by more than rounding anywhere, even by a few dots, is not used; pages with embedded fonts that are drawn slightly differently when copied (TeX, for example) keep the whole document. Of a TIFF with several pages only the chosen page is kept."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Opening PDF files needs Poppler (poppler-glib); the Flatpak brings it along, otherwise install it from your distribution (see the README)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/use.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Most shipping label rolls are direct thermal labels: they need no ribbon, but the print fades in heat and sunlight within months. That is fine for a parcel on its way; for labels that must last, use thermal transfer labels with a ribbon."
msgstr ""

